{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"tft-displays","name":"Colour TFT screens","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Full-colour SPI screens: the 1.8\" ST7735 (128 x 160) and the 2.8\" ILI9341 (240 x 320). Draw shapes, text and pictures with the Adafruit GFX functions. Includes Adafruit_ST7735.h, Adafruit_ILI9341.h, Adafruit_ST7789.h and Adafruit_GFX.h.","category":"Displays","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// Colour TFTs (ST7735 128x160, ILI9341 240x320): the controller's commands over SPI, DC telling\r\n// commands (LOW) from their data (HIGH). CASET / RASET set a window; RAMWR's data fills it with RGB565\r\n// pixels, left to right, top to bottom. MADCTL turns and mirrors how the window lands on the glass.\r\nconst tft = (W, H) => (part) => {\r\n  const screen = part.screen('tft');\r\n  let powered = false, on = false, asleep = true, cmd = -1, args = [], x0 = 0, x1 = W - 1, y0 = 0, y1 = H - 1, cx = 0, cy = 0, mad = 0, inv = false, pending = -1, pixels = 0, hi = -1;\r\n  const reset = () => {\r\n    on = false; asleep = true; cmd = -1; args = []; mad = 0; inv = false; hi = -1;\r\n    x0 = 0; x1 = W - 1; y0 = 0; y1 = H - 1;\r\n    screen.fill(0);\r\n  };\r\n  // a pixel of the window (column c, row r) onto the glass\r\n  const put = (c, r, rgb565) => {\r\n    const mv = mad & 0x20, mx = mad & 0x40, my = mad & 0x80;\r\n    const lw = mv ? H : W, lh = mv ? W : H;\r\n    if (c >= lw || r >= lh) return;\r\n    let a = mx ? lw - 1 - c : c, b = my ? lh - 1 - r : r;\r\n    const px = mv ? b : a, py = mv ? a : b;\r\n    let red = (rgb565 >> 11) & 31, green = (rgb565 >> 5) & 63, blue = rgb565 & 31;\r\n    if (!(mad & 0x08)) { const t = red; red = blue; blue = t; } // (the glass is BGR: the BGR bit says so, else colours swap)\r\n    let rgb = (((red * 527 + 23) >> 6) << 16) | (((green * 259 + 33) >> 6) << 8) | ((blue * 527 + 23) >> 6);\r\n    if (inv) rgb ^= 0xffffff;\r\n    screen.set(px, py, rgb);\r\n    pixels++;\r\n  };\r\n  const data = (b) => {\r\n    if (cmd === 0x2c) {\r\n      if (hi < 0) { hi = b; return; }\r\n      const v = (hi << 8) | b;\r\n      hi = -1;\r\n      put(cx, cy, v);\r\n      if (++cx > x1) { cx = x0; if (++cy > y1) cy = y0; }\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n    args.push(b);\r\n    if (cmd === 0x2a && args.length === 4) { x0 = (args[0] << 8) | args[1]; x1 = (args[2] << 8) | args[3]; }\r\n    else if (cmd === 0x2b && args.length === 4) { y0 = (args[0] << 8) | args[1]; y1 = (args[2] << 8) | args[3]; }\r\n    else if (cmd === 0x36 && args.length === 1) mad = b;\r\n  };\r\n  const command = (c) => {\r\n    cmd = c; args = []; hi = -1;\r\n    if (c === 0x01) reset();\r\n    else if (c === 0x11) asleep = false;\r\n    else if (c === 0x10) asleep = true;\r\n    else if (c === 0x29) on = true;\r\n    else if (c === 0x28) on = false;\r\n    else if (c === 0x20) inv = false;\r\n    else if (c === 0x21) inv = true;\r\n    else if (c === 0x2c) { cx = x0; cy = y0; }\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    spi: {\r\n      transfer(bytes, pins) {\r\n        if (!powered) return;\r\n        if ((pins.DC ?? pins.A0) === 0) for (const b of bytes) command(b);\r\n        else for (const b of bytes) data(b);\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      const now = v >= 2.8 && io.level('RESET') !== 0;\r\n      if (now && !powered) reset();\r\n      if (!now && powered) screen.fill(0);\r\n      powered = now;\r\n      // (its backlight: LED pin HIGH, or unwired)\r\n      screen.light(powered && on && !asleep && io.level('LED') !== 0);\r\n      io.draw(powered ? 0.02 + (io.level('LED') !== 0 ? 0.04 : 0) : 0);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VCC, RST high)'];\r\n      return [`${on && !asleep ? 'on' : asleep ? 'asleep (not started: tft.initR() / tft.begin())' : 'display off'}${inv ? ', inverted' : ''}`, `${pixels} pixels drawn`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n};\r\nbench.device('st7735', tft(128, 160));\r\nbench.device('ili9341', tft(240, 320));\r\n","sketch":{"Adafruit_ST7735.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_ST7735"],"exports":["ST77XX_BLACK","ST77XX_WHITE","ST77XX_RED","ST77XX_GREEN","ST77XX_BLUE","ST77XX_CYAN","ST77XX_MAGENTA","ST77XX_YELLOW","ST77XX_ORANGE","ST7735_BLACK","ST7735_WHITE","ST7735_RED","ST7735_GREEN","ST7735_BLUE","ST7735_CYAN","ST7735_MAGENTA","ST7735_YELLOW","ST7735_ORANGE","INITR_GREENTAB","INITR_REDTAB","INITR_BLACKTAB","INITR_144GREENTAB","INITR_MINI160x80"],"code":"// Colour TFT screens (Adafruit_ST7735.h, Adafruit_ILI9341.h, Adafruit_ST7789.h) and the Adafruit_GFX\r\n// drawing they share: fillScreen(), drawPixel(), drawLine(), drawRect(), fillRect(), drawCircle(),\r\n// fillCircle(), drawRoundRect(), drawTriangle(), setCursor(), setTextColor(c, bg), setTextSize(),\r\n// print(), setRotation(), color565(r, g, b).\r\n//   Adafruit_ST7735 tft = Adafruit_ST7735(TFT_CS, TFT_DC, TFT_RST);  tft.initR(INITR_BLACKTAB);\r\n//   Adafruit_ILI9341 tft = Adafruit_ILI9341(TFT_CS, TFT_DC);  tft.begin();\r\n// the classic 5x7 font, ASCII 32-126: five columns per character, bit 0 = the top row\r\nconst FONT5X7 = [\r\n  0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x5f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x24, 0x2a, 0x7f, 0x2a, 0x12, 0x23, 0x13, 0x08, 0x64, 0x62, 0x36, 0x49, 0x55, 0x22, 0x50, 0x00, 0x05, 0x03, 0x00, 0x00,\r\n  0x00, 0x1c, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x00, 0x08, 0x2a, 0x1c, 0x2a, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x3e, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x50, 0x30, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x60, 0x60, 0x00, 0x00, 0x20, 0x10, 0x08, 0x04, 0x02,\r\n  0x3e, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x3e, 0x00, 0x42, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x42, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x46, 0x21, 0x41, 0x45, 0x4b, 0x31, 0x18, 0x14, 0x12, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x27, 0x45, 0x45, 0x45, 0x39, 0x3c, 0x4a, 0x49, 0x49, 0x30, 0x01, 0x71, 0x09, 0x05, 0x03,\r\n  0x36, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x06, 0x49, 0x49, 0x29, 0x1e, 0x00, 0x36, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x56, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x14, 0x08, 0x02, 0x01, 0x51, 0x09, 0x06,\r\n  0x32, 0x49, 0x79, 0x41, 0x3e, 0x7e, 0x11, 0x11, 0x11, 0x7e, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x01, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x49, 0x49, 0x7a,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x41, 0x3f, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x7f, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x02, 0x7f, 0x7f, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x7f, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x51, 0x21, 0x5e, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x19, 0x29, 0x46, 0x46, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x31, 0x01, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x01, 0x01, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x3f, 0x1f, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1f, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x38, 0x40, 0x3f,\r\n  0x63, 0x14, 0x08, 0x14, 0x63, 0x07, 0x08, 0x70, 0x08, 0x07, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x43, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x00, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x20, 0x00, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x04, 0x02, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40,\r\n  0x00, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x00, 0x20, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x78, 0x7f, 0x48, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x20, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x48, 0x7f, 0x38, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x18, 0x08, 0x7e, 0x09, 0x01, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x52, 0x52, 0x52, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x00, 0x44, 0x7d, 0x40, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x44, 0x3d, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x7c, 0x04, 0x18, 0x04, 0x78, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38,\r\n  0x7c, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x08, 0x08, 0x14, 0x14, 0x18, 0x7c, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x08, 0x48, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x20, 0x04, 0x3f, 0x44, 0x40, 0x20, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x40, 0x20, 0x7c, 0x1c, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1c, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x30, 0x40, 0x3c,\r\n  0x44, 0x28, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x0c, 0x50, 0x50, 0x50, 0x3c, 0x44, 0x64, 0x54, 0x4c, 0x44, 0x00, 0x08, 0x36, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x36, 0x08, 0x00, 0x08, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x08,\r\n];\r\nconst DEGREE = [0x00, 0x06, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06]; // (char)247 / (char)176: a degree sign\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h) {\r\n    this.WIDTH = w;\r\n    this.HEIGHT = h;\r\n    this._width = w;\r\n    this._height = h;\r\n    this.rotation = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_x = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_y = 0;\r\n    this.textsize_x = 1;\r\n    this.textsize_y = 1;\r\n    this.textcolor = 1;\r\n    this.textbgcolor = 1;\r\n    this.wrap = true;\r\n  }\r\n  width() { return this._width; }\r\n  height() { return this._height; }\r\n  getRotation() { return this.rotation; }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    this.rotation = r & 3;\r\n    const swap = this.rotation & 1;\r\n    this._width = swap ? this.HEIGHT : this.WIDTH;\r\n    this._height = swap ? this.WIDTH : this.HEIGHT;\r\n  }\r\n  setCursor(x, y) { this.cursor_x = Math.trunc(x); this.cursor_y = Math.trunc(y); }\r\n  getCursorX() { return this.cursor_x; }\r\n  getCursorY() { return this.cursor_y; }\r\n  setTextSize(sx, sy) { this.textsize_x = Math.max(1, sx | 0); this.textsize_y = Math.max(1, (sy ?? sx) | 0); }\r\n  setTextColor(c, bg) { this.textcolor = c; this.textbgcolor = bg === undefined ? c : bg; }\r\n  setTextWrap(w) { this.wrap = !!w; }\r\n  cp437() {}\r\n  setFont() {}\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  writePixel(x, y, c) { this.drawPixel(x, y, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < h; i++) this.drawPixel(x, y + i, c); }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y, c); }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawFastVLine(x + i, y, h, c); }\r\n  drawRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y + h - 1, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y, h, c);\r\n  }\r\n  drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c) {\r\n    x0 = Math.round(x0); y0 = Math.round(y0); x1 = Math.round(x1); y1 = Math.round(y1);\r\n    const dx = Math.abs(x1 - x0), dy = -Math.abs(y1 - y0), sx = x0 < x1 ? 1 : -1, sy = y0 < y1 ? 1 : -1;\r\n    let err = dx + dy;\r\n    for (;;) {\r\n      this.drawPixel(x0, y0, c);\r\n      if (x0 === x1 && y0 === y1) break;\r\n      const e2 = 2 * err;\r\n      if (e2 >= dy) { err += dy; x0 += sx; }\r\n      if (e2 <= dx) { err += dx; y0 += sy; }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    let f = 1 - r, ddx = 1, ddy = -2 * r, x = 0, y = r;\r\n    this.drawPixel(x0, y0 + r, c); this.drawPixel(x0, y0 - r, c); this.drawPixel(x0 + r, y0, c); this.drawPixel(x0 - r, y0, c);\r\n    while (x < y) {\r\n      if (f >= 0) { y--; ddy += 2; f += ddy; }\r\n      x++; ddx += 2; f += ddx;\r\n      for (const [a, b] of [[x, y], [y, x], [-x, y], [-y, x], [x, -y], [y, -x], [-x, -y], [-y, -x]]) this.drawPixel(x0 + a, y0 + b, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    for (let y = -r; y <= r; y++) {\r\n      const w = Math.floor(Math.sqrt(r * r - y * y));\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x0 - w, y0 + y, 2 * w + 1, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y + h - 1, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    for (let a = 0; a <= 90; a += 3) {\r\n      const dx = Math.round(r - r * Math.cos((a * Math.PI) / 180)), dy = Math.round(r - r * Math.sin((a * Math.PI) / 180));\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + dy, c);\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) {\r\n      const d = j < r ? r - j : j >= h - r ? j - (h - 1 - r) : 0;\r\n      const inset = d ? Math.round(r - Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, r * r - d * d))) : 0;\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x + inset, y + j, w - 2 * inset, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    this.drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x1, y1, x2, y2, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x2, y2, x0, y0, c);\r\n  }\r\n  fillTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    const minY = Math.min(y0, y1, y2), maxY = Math.max(y0, y1, y2);\r\n    const edges = [[x0, y0, x1, y1], [x1, y1, x2, y2], [x2, y2, x0, y0]];\r\n    for (let y = minY; y <= maxY; y++) {\r\n      const xs = [];\r\n      for (const [ax, ay, bx, by] of edges) if ((y >= Math.min(ay, by)) && (y <= Math.max(ay, by)) && ay !== by) xs.push(ax + ((y - ay) * (bx - ax)) / (by - ay));\r\n      if (xs.length >= 2) { const a = Math.round(Math.min(...xs)), b = Math.round(Math.max(...xs)); this.drawFastHLine(a, y, b - a + 1, c); }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  /** a bitmap: rows of bytes, the leftmost pixel in the top bit (as the Adafruit examples' arrays) */\r\n  drawBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h, c, bg) {\r\n    const bw = Math.floor((w + 7) / 8);\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++)\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) {\r\n        const on = (bmp[j * bw + (i >> 3)] << (i & 7)) & 0x80;\r\n        if (on) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== undefined) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bg);\r\n      }\r\n  }\r\n  drawChar(x, y, ch, c, bg, sx, sy = sx) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    const g = code === 247 || code === 176 ? DEGREE : code >= 32 && code <= 126 ? FONT5X7.slice((code - 32) * 5, (code - 32) * 5 + 5) : [0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f];\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\r\n      const col = i < 5 ? g[i] : 0;\r\n      for (let j = 0; j < 8; j++) {\r\n        const on = (col >> j) & 1;\r\n        if (on) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== c) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, bg);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  write(ch) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    if (code === 10) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; return 1; }\r\n    if (code === 13) return 1;\r\n    if (this.wrap && this.cursor_x + this.textsize_x * 6 > this._width) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; }\r\n    this.drawChar(this.cursor_x, this.cursor_y, code, this.textcolor, this.textbgcolor, this.textsize_x, this.textsize_y);\r\n    this.cursor_x += this.textsize_x * 6;\r\n    return 1;\r\n  }\r\n  print(x = '', f) {\r\n    let s;\r\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && f !== undefined) s = f === 16 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(16).toUpperCase() : f === 2 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(2) : f === 8 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(8) : f === 10 ? String(Math.trunc(x)) : x.toFixed(f);\r\n    else if (typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x)) s = x.toFixed(2);\r\n    else s = String(x);\r\n    for (const ch of s) this.write(ch.charCodeAt(0) > 255 ? 63 : ch.charCodeAt(0));\r\n    return s.length;\r\n  }\r\n  println(x = '', f) { const n = this.print(x, f); this.write(10); return n + 1; }\r\n  printf(fmt, ...a) {\r\n    this.print(String(fmt).replace(/%(-?\\d*)(?:\\.(\\d+))?([dfsxXcu%])/g, (_m, w, p, t) => {\r\n      if (t === '%') return '%';\r\n      const v = a.shift();\r\n      let s = t === 'f' ? Number(v).toFixed(p ? Number(p) : 6) : t === 'x' ? Number(v).toString(16) : t === 'X' ? Number(v).toString(16).toUpperCase() : t === 'c' ? String.fromCharCode(v) : t === 'd' || t === 'u' ? String(Math.trunc(v)) : String(v);\r\n      const width = Math.abs(Number(w || 0));\r\n      if (s.length < width) s = w.startsWith('-') ? s.padEnd(width) : s.padStart(width, w.startsWith('0') ? '0' : ' ');\r\n      return s;\r\n    }));\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// The TFT drivers. Like the real libraries they talk to the controller chip over SPI: commands with\r\n// DC LOW, their data with DC HIGH (CASET / RASET set a window, RAMWR fills it with RGB565 pixels).\r\n// To be quick they draw each call (a rectangle, a line, a line of text) on the board first and send\r\n// the changed area at once, instead of pixel by pixel.\r\nconst ST77XX_BLACK = 0x0000, ST77XX_WHITE = 0xffff, ST77XX_RED = 0xf800, ST77XX_GREEN = 0x07e0, ST77XX_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ST77XX_CYAN = 0x07ff, ST77XX_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ST77XX_YELLOW = 0xffe0, ST77XX_ORANGE = 0xfc00;\r\nconst ST7735_BLACK = ST77XX_BLACK, ST7735_WHITE = ST77XX_WHITE, ST7735_RED = ST77XX_RED, ST7735_GREEN = ST77XX_GREEN, ST7735_BLUE = ST77XX_BLUE;\r\nconst ST7735_CYAN = ST77XX_CYAN, ST7735_MAGENTA = ST77XX_MAGENTA, ST7735_YELLOW = ST77XX_YELLOW, ST7735_ORANGE = ST77XX_ORANGE;\r\nconst ILI9341_BLACK = 0x0000, ILI9341_NAVY = 0x000f, ILI9341_DARKGREEN = 0x03e0, ILI9341_DARKCYAN = 0x03ef, ILI9341_MAROON = 0x7800;\r\nconst ILI9341_PURPLE = 0x780f, ILI9341_OLIVE = 0x7be0, ILI9341_LIGHTGREY = 0xc618, ILI9341_DARKGREY = 0x7bef, ILI9341_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ILI9341_GREEN = 0x07e0, ILI9341_CYAN = 0x07ff, ILI9341_RED = 0xf800, ILI9341_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ILI9341_YELLOW = 0xffe0;\r\nconst ILI9341_WHITE = 0xffff, ILI9341_ORANGE = 0xfd20, ILI9341_GREENYELLOW = 0xafe5, ILI9341_PINK = 0xfc18;\r\nconst INITR_GREENTAB = 0x00, INITR_REDTAB = 0x01, INITR_BLACKTAB = 0x02, INITR_144GREENTAB = 0x01, INITR_MINI160x80 = 0x04;\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_SPITFT extends Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h, cs, dc, a, b, c) {\r\n    super(w, h);\r\n    this.cs = cs; this.dc = dc;\r\n    // (cs, dc, rst) for hardware SPI; (cs, dc, mosi, sclk, rst) for software SPI: the same here\r\n    this.rst = c !== undefined ? c : a !== undefined && b === undefined ? a : -1;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(w * h);\r\n    this.fbw = w;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    this.depth = 0;\r\n    this.textcolor = 0xffff; this.textbgcolor = 0xffff;\r\n    // each drawing call sends what it changed when it's done (calls inside calls wait for the outer one)\r\n    for (const m of ['fillScreen', 'fillRect', 'drawRect', 'drawLine', 'drawFastHLine', 'drawFastVLine', 'drawPixel', 'drawCircle', 'fillCircle', 'drawRoundRect', 'fillRoundRect', 'drawTriangle', 'fillTriangle', 'drawBitmap', 'drawRGBBitmap', 'drawChar', 'write', 'print', 'println', 'printf']) {\r\n      const f = this[m];\r\n      this[m] = (...args) => {\r\n        this.depth++;\r\n        try { return f.apply(this, args); } finally { if (--this.depth === 0) this._flush(); }\r\n      };\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  _send(cmd, data) {\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([cmd]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    if (data && data.length) SPI.writeBytes(data);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n  _start() {\r\n    pinMode(this.cs, OUTPUT); pinMode(this.dc, OUTPUT);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n    if (this.rst >= 0) { pinMode(this.rst, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, LOW); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(20); }\r\n    SPI.begin();\r\n    this._send(0x01); delay(50);      // SWRESET\r\n    this._send(0x11); delay(50);      // SLPOUT\r\n    this._send(0x3a, [0x55]);         // COLMOD: 16 bits a pixel\r\n    this.setRotation(0);\r\n    this._send(0x29);                 // DISPON\r\n  }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    super.setRotation(r);\r\n    const MAD = [0x00, 0x60, 0xc0, 0xa0][this.rotation]; // (MY MX MV: how the window maps onto the glass)\r\n    this._send(0x36, [MAD | 0x08]);   // (+ BGR order, as these panels are)\r\n    this.fbw = this._width;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(this._width * this._height);\r\n  }\r\n  drawPixel(x, y, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y);\r\n    if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= this._width || y >= this._height) return;\r\n    this.fb[y * this.fbw + x] = c & 0xffff;\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x, y, x, y];\r\n    else { if (x < d[0]) d[0] = x; if (y < d[1]) d[1] = y; if (x > d[2]) d[2] = x; if (y > d[3]) d[3] = y; }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y); w = Math.trunc(w); h = Math.trunc(h);\r\n    if (w < 0) { x += w; w = -w; }\r\n    if (h < 0) { y += h; h = -h; }\r\n    const x0 = Math.max(0, x), y0 = Math.max(0, y), x1 = Math.min(this._width, x + w), y1 = Math.min(this._height, y + h);\r\n    if (x1 <= x0 || y1 <= y0) return;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j < y1; j++) this.fb.fill(c & 0xffff, j * this.fbw + x0, j * this.fbw + x1);\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x0, y0, x1 - 1, y1 - 1];\r\n    else { d[0] = Math.min(d[0], x0); d[1] = Math.min(d[1], y0); d[2] = Math.max(d[2], x1 - 1); d[3] = Math.max(d[3], y1 - 1); }\r\n  }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, w, 1, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, 1, h, c); }\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  /** a 16-bit colour from red, green, blue (0-255) */\r\n  color565(r, g, b) { return ((r & 0xf8) << 8) | ((g & 0xfc) << 3) | (b >> 3); }\r\n  drawRGBBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h) { for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bmp[j * w + i]); }\r\n  invertDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x21 : 0x20); }\r\n  enableDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x29 : 0x28); }\r\n  enableSleep(on) { this._send(on ? 0x10 : 0x11); }\r\n  setAddrWindow(x, y, w, h) {\r\n    this._send(0x2a, [x >> 8, x & 255, (x + w - 1) >> 8, (x + w - 1) & 255]);\r\n    this._send(0x2b, [y >> 8, y & 255, (y + h - 1) >> 8, (y + h - 1) & 255]);\r\n  }\r\n  startWrite() {}\r\n  endWrite() {}\r\n  /** the changed area, sent: a window, then its pixels (two bytes each, high byte first) */\r\n  _flush() {\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) return;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    const [x0, y0, x1, y1] = d;\r\n    const w = x1 - x0 + 1, h = y1 - y0 + 1;\r\n    this.setAddrWindow(x0, y0, w, h);\r\n    const px = new Array(w * h * 2);\r\n    let k = 0;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j <= y1; j++)\r\n      for (let i = x0; i <= x1; i++) { const c = this.fb[j * this.fbw + i]; px[k++] = c >> 8; px[k++] = c & 255; }\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([0x2c]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes(px);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7735 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(128, 160, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  initR(tab = INITR_BLACKTAB) { if (tab === INITR_MINI160x80) { this.WIDTH = 80; this.HEIGHT = 160; } this._start(); }\r\n  initB() { this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7789 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  init(w = 240, h = 320) { this.WIDTH = w; this.HEIGHT = h; this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ILI9341 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  begin() { this._start(); }\r\n  readcommand8() { return 0; }\r\n}\r\n"},"Adafruit_ST7789.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_ST7789"],"exports":["ST77XX_BLACK","ST77XX_WHITE","ST77XX_RED","ST77XX_GREEN","ST77XX_BLUE","ST77XX_CYAN","ST77XX_MAGENTA","ST77XX_YELLOW","ST77XX_ORANGE"],"code":"// Colour TFT screens (Adafruit_ST7735.h, Adafruit_ILI9341.h, Adafruit_ST7789.h) and the Adafruit_GFX\r\n// drawing they share: fillScreen(), drawPixel(), drawLine(), drawRect(), fillRect(), drawCircle(),\r\n// fillCircle(), drawRoundRect(), drawTriangle(), setCursor(), setTextColor(c, bg), setTextSize(),\r\n// print(), setRotation(), color565(r, g, b).\r\n//   Adafruit_ST7735 tft = Adafruit_ST7735(TFT_CS, TFT_DC, TFT_RST);  tft.initR(INITR_BLACKTAB);\r\n//   Adafruit_ILI9341 tft = Adafruit_ILI9341(TFT_CS, TFT_DC);  tft.begin();\r\n// the classic 5x7 font, ASCII 32-126: five columns per character, bit 0 = the top row\r\nconst FONT5X7 = [\r\n  0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x5f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x24, 0x2a, 0x7f, 0x2a, 0x12, 0x23, 0x13, 0x08, 0x64, 0x62, 0x36, 0x49, 0x55, 0x22, 0x50, 0x00, 0x05, 0x03, 0x00, 0x00,\r\n  0x00, 0x1c, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x00, 0x08, 0x2a, 0x1c, 0x2a, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x3e, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x50, 0x30, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x60, 0x60, 0x00, 0x00, 0x20, 0x10, 0x08, 0x04, 0x02,\r\n  0x3e, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x3e, 0x00, 0x42, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x42, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x46, 0x21, 0x41, 0x45, 0x4b, 0x31, 0x18, 0x14, 0x12, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x27, 0x45, 0x45, 0x45, 0x39, 0x3c, 0x4a, 0x49, 0x49, 0x30, 0x01, 0x71, 0x09, 0x05, 0x03,\r\n  0x36, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x06, 0x49, 0x49, 0x29, 0x1e, 0x00, 0x36, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x56, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x14, 0x08, 0x02, 0x01, 0x51, 0x09, 0x06,\r\n  0x32, 0x49, 0x79, 0x41, 0x3e, 0x7e, 0x11, 0x11, 0x11, 0x7e, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x01, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x49, 0x49, 0x7a,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x41, 0x3f, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x7f, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x02, 0x7f, 0x7f, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x7f, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x51, 0x21, 0x5e, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x19, 0x29, 0x46, 0x46, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x31, 0x01, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x01, 0x01, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x3f, 0x1f, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1f, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x38, 0x40, 0x3f,\r\n  0x63, 0x14, 0x08, 0x14, 0x63, 0x07, 0x08, 0x70, 0x08, 0x07, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x43, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x00, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x20, 0x00, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x04, 0x02, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40,\r\n  0x00, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x00, 0x20, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x78, 0x7f, 0x48, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x20, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x48, 0x7f, 0x38, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x18, 0x08, 0x7e, 0x09, 0x01, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x52, 0x52, 0x52, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x00, 0x44, 0x7d, 0x40, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x44, 0x3d, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x7c, 0x04, 0x18, 0x04, 0x78, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38,\r\n  0x7c, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x08, 0x08, 0x14, 0x14, 0x18, 0x7c, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x08, 0x48, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x20, 0x04, 0x3f, 0x44, 0x40, 0x20, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x40, 0x20, 0x7c, 0x1c, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1c, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x30, 0x40, 0x3c,\r\n  0x44, 0x28, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x0c, 0x50, 0x50, 0x50, 0x3c, 0x44, 0x64, 0x54, 0x4c, 0x44, 0x00, 0x08, 0x36, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x36, 0x08, 0x00, 0x08, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x08,\r\n];\r\nconst DEGREE = [0x00, 0x06, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06]; // (char)247 / (char)176: a degree sign\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h) {\r\n    this.WIDTH = w;\r\n    this.HEIGHT = h;\r\n    this._width = w;\r\n    this._height = h;\r\n    this.rotation = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_x = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_y = 0;\r\n    this.textsize_x = 1;\r\n    this.textsize_y = 1;\r\n    this.textcolor = 1;\r\n    this.textbgcolor = 1;\r\n    this.wrap = true;\r\n  }\r\n  width() { return this._width; }\r\n  height() { return this._height; }\r\n  getRotation() { return this.rotation; }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    this.rotation = r & 3;\r\n    const swap = this.rotation & 1;\r\n    this._width = swap ? this.HEIGHT : this.WIDTH;\r\n    this._height = swap ? this.WIDTH : this.HEIGHT;\r\n  }\r\n  setCursor(x, y) { this.cursor_x = Math.trunc(x); this.cursor_y = Math.trunc(y); }\r\n  getCursorX() { return this.cursor_x; }\r\n  getCursorY() { return this.cursor_y; }\r\n  setTextSize(sx, sy) { this.textsize_x = Math.max(1, sx | 0); this.textsize_y = Math.max(1, (sy ?? sx) | 0); }\r\n  setTextColor(c, bg) { this.textcolor = c; this.textbgcolor = bg === undefined ? c : bg; }\r\n  setTextWrap(w) { this.wrap = !!w; }\r\n  cp437() {}\r\n  setFont() {}\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  writePixel(x, y, c) { this.drawPixel(x, y, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < h; i++) this.drawPixel(x, y + i, c); }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y, c); }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawFastVLine(x + i, y, h, c); }\r\n  drawRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y + h - 1, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y, h, c);\r\n  }\r\n  drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c) {\r\n    x0 = Math.round(x0); y0 = Math.round(y0); x1 = Math.round(x1); y1 = Math.round(y1);\r\n    const dx = Math.abs(x1 - x0), dy = -Math.abs(y1 - y0), sx = x0 < x1 ? 1 : -1, sy = y0 < y1 ? 1 : -1;\r\n    let err = dx + dy;\r\n    for (;;) {\r\n      this.drawPixel(x0, y0, c);\r\n      if (x0 === x1 && y0 === y1) break;\r\n      const e2 = 2 * err;\r\n      if (e2 >= dy) { err += dy; x0 += sx; }\r\n      if (e2 <= dx) { err += dx; y0 += sy; }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    let f = 1 - r, ddx = 1, ddy = -2 * r, x = 0, y = r;\r\n    this.drawPixel(x0, y0 + r, c); this.drawPixel(x0, y0 - r, c); this.drawPixel(x0 + r, y0, c); this.drawPixel(x0 - r, y0, c);\r\n    while (x < y) {\r\n      if (f >= 0) { y--; ddy += 2; f += ddy; }\r\n      x++; ddx += 2; f += ddx;\r\n      for (const [a, b] of [[x, y], [y, x], [-x, y], [-y, x], [x, -y], [y, -x], [-x, -y], [-y, -x]]) this.drawPixel(x0 + a, y0 + b, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    for (let y = -r; y <= r; y++) {\r\n      const w = Math.floor(Math.sqrt(r * r - y * y));\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x0 - w, y0 + y, 2 * w + 1, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y + h - 1, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    for (let a = 0; a <= 90; a += 3) {\r\n      const dx = Math.round(r - r * Math.cos((a * Math.PI) / 180)), dy = Math.round(r - r * Math.sin((a * Math.PI) / 180));\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + dy, c);\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) {\r\n      const d = j < r ? r - j : j >= h - r ? j - (h - 1 - r) : 0;\r\n      const inset = d ? Math.round(r - Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, r * r - d * d))) : 0;\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x + inset, y + j, w - 2 * inset, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    this.drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x1, y1, x2, y2, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x2, y2, x0, y0, c);\r\n  }\r\n  fillTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    const minY = Math.min(y0, y1, y2), maxY = Math.max(y0, y1, y2);\r\n    const edges = [[x0, y0, x1, y1], [x1, y1, x2, y2], [x2, y2, x0, y0]];\r\n    for (let y = minY; y <= maxY; y++) {\r\n      const xs = [];\r\n      for (const [ax, ay, bx, by] of edges) if ((y >= Math.min(ay, by)) && (y <= Math.max(ay, by)) && ay !== by) xs.push(ax + ((y - ay) * (bx - ax)) / (by - ay));\r\n      if (xs.length >= 2) { const a = Math.round(Math.min(...xs)), b = Math.round(Math.max(...xs)); this.drawFastHLine(a, y, b - a + 1, c); }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  /** a bitmap: rows of bytes, the leftmost pixel in the top bit (as the Adafruit examples' arrays) */\r\n  drawBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h, c, bg) {\r\n    const bw = Math.floor((w + 7) / 8);\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++)\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) {\r\n        const on = (bmp[j * bw + (i >> 3)] << (i & 7)) & 0x80;\r\n        if (on) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== undefined) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bg);\r\n      }\r\n  }\r\n  drawChar(x, y, ch, c, bg, sx, sy = sx) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    const g = code === 247 || code === 176 ? DEGREE : code >= 32 && code <= 126 ? FONT5X7.slice((code - 32) * 5, (code - 32) * 5 + 5) : [0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f];\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\r\n      const col = i < 5 ? g[i] : 0;\r\n      for (let j = 0; j < 8; j++) {\r\n        const on = (col >> j) & 1;\r\n        if (on) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== c) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, bg);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  write(ch) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    if (code === 10) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; return 1; }\r\n    if (code === 13) return 1;\r\n    if (this.wrap && this.cursor_x + this.textsize_x * 6 > this._width) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; }\r\n    this.drawChar(this.cursor_x, this.cursor_y, code, this.textcolor, this.textbgcolor, this.textsize_x, this.textsize_y);\r\n    this.cursor_x += this.textsize_x * 6;\r\n    return 1;\r\n  }\r\n  print(x = '', f) {\r\n    let s;\r\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && f !== undefined) s = f === 16 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(16).toUpperCase() : f === 2 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(2) : f === 8 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(8) : f === 10 ? String(Math.trunc(x)) : x.toFixed(f);\r\n    else if (typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x)) s = x.toFixed(2);\r\n    else s = String(x);\r\n    for (const ch of s) this.write(ch.charCodeAt(0) > 255 ? 63 : ch.charCodeAt(0));\r\n    return s.length;\r\n  }\r\n  println(x = '', f) { const n = this.print(x, f); this.write(10); return n + 1; }\r\n  printf(fmt, ...a) {\r\n    this.print(String(fmt).replace(/%(-?\\d*)(?:\\.(\\d+))?([dfsxXcu%])/g, (_m, w, p, t) => {\r\n      if (t === '%') return '%';\r\n      const v = a.shift();\r\n      let s = t === 'f' ? Number(v).toFixed(p ? Number(p) : 6) : t === 'x' ? Number(v).toString(16) : t === 'X' ? Number(v).toString(16).toUpperCase() : t === 'c' ? String.fromCharCode(v) : t === 'd' || t === 'u' ? String(Math.trunc(v)) : String(v);\r\n      const width = Math.abs(Number(w || 0));\r\n      if (s.length < width) s = w.startsWith('-') ? s.padEnd(width) : s.padStart(width, w.startsWith('0') ? '0' : ' ');\r\n      return s;\r\n    }));\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// The TFT drivers. Like the real libraries they talk to the controller chip over SPI: commands with\r\n// DC LOW, their data with DC HIGH (CASET / RASET set a window, RAMWR fills it with RGB565 pixels).\r\n// To be quick they draw each call (a rectangle, a line, a line of text) on the board first and send\r\n// the changed area at once, instead of pixel by pixel.\r\nconst ST77XX_BLACK = 0x0000, ST77XX_WHITE = 0xffff, ST77XX_RED = 0xf800, ST77XX_GREEN = 0x07e0, ST77XX_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ST77XX_CYAN = 0x07ff, ST77XX_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ST77XX_YELLOW = 0xffe0, ST77XX_ORANGE = 0xfc00;\r\nconst ST7735_BLACK = ST77XX_BLACK, ST7735_WHITE = ST77XX_WHITE, ST7735_RED = ST77XX_RED, ST7735_GREEN = ST77XX_GREEN, ST7735_BLUE = ST77XX_BLUE;\r\nconst ST7735_CYAN = ST77XX_CYAN, ST7735_MAGENTA = ST77XX_MAGENTA, ST7735_YELLOW = ST77XX_YELLOW, ST7735_ORANGE = ST77XX_ORANGE;\r\nconst ILI9341_BLACK = 0x0000, ILI9341_NAVY = 0x000f, ILI9341_DARKGREEN = 0x03e0, ILI9341_DARKCYAN = 0x03ef, ILI9341_MAROON = 0x7800;\r\nconst ILI9341_PURPLE = 0x780f, ILI9341_OLIVE = 0x7be0, ILI9341_LIGHTGREY = 0xc618, ILI9341_DARKGREY = 0x7bef, ILI9341_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ILI9341_GREEN = 0x07e0, ILI9341_CYAN = 0x07ff, ILI9341_RED = 0xf800, ILI9341_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ILI9341_YELLOW = 0xffe0;\r\nconst ILI9341_WHITE = 0xffff, ILI9341_ORANGE = 0xfd20, ILI9341_GREENYELLOW = 0xafe5, ILI9341_PINK = 0xfc18;\r\nconst INITR_GREENTAB = 0x00, INITR_REDTAB = 0x01, INITR_BLACKTAB = 0x02, INITR_144GREENTAB = 0x01, INITR_MINI160x80 = 0x04;\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_SPITFT extends Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h, cs, dc, a, b, c) {\r\n    super(w, h);\r\n    this.cs = cs; this.dc = dc;\r\n    // (cs, dc, rst) for hardware SPI; (cs, dc, mosi, sclk, rst) for software SPI: the same here\r\n    this.rst = c !== undefined ? c : a !== undefined && b === undefined ? a : -1;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(w * h);\r\n    this.fbw = w;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    this.depth = 0;\r\n    this.textcolor = 0xffff; this.textbgcolor = 0xffff;\r\n    // each drawing call sends what it changed when it's done (calls inside calls wait for the outer one)\r\n    for (const m of ['fillScreen', 'fillRect', 'drawRect', 'drawLine', 'drawFastHLine', 'drawFastVLine', 'drawPixel', 'drawCircle', 'fillCircle', 'drawRoundRect', 'fillRoundRect', 'drawTriangle', 'fillTriangle', 'drawBitmap', 'drawRGBBitmap', 'drawChar', 'write', 'print', 'println', 'printf']) {\r\n      const f = this[m];\r\n      this[m] = (...args) => {\r\n        this.depth++;\r\n        try { return f.apply(this, args); } finally { if (--this.depth === 0) this._flush(); }\r\n      };\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  _send(cmd, data) {\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([cmd]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    if (data && data.length) SPI.writeBytes(data);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n  _start() {\r\n    pinMode(this.cs, OUTPUT); pinMode(this.dc, OUTPUT);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n    if (this.rst >= 0) { pinMode(this.rst, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, LOW); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(20); }\r\n    SPI.begin();\r\n    this._send(0x01); delay(50);      // SWRESET\r\n    this._send(0x11); delay(50);      // SLPOUT\r\n    this._send(0x3a, [0x55]);         // COLMOD: 16 bits a pixel\r\n    this.setRotation(0);\r\n    this._send(0x29);                 // DISPON\r\n  }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    super.setRotation(r);\r\n    const MAD = [0x00, 0x60, 0xc0, 0xa0][this.rotation]; // (MY MX MV: how the window maps onto the glass)\r\n    this._send(0x36, [MAD | 0x08]);   // (+ BGR order, as these panels are)\r\n    this.fbw = this._width;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(this._width * this._height);\r\n  }\r\n  drawPixel(x, y, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y);\r\n    if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= this._width || y >= this._height) return;\r\n    this.fb[y * this.fbw + x] = c & 0xffff;\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x, y, x, y];\r\n    else { if (x < d[0]) d[0] = x; if (y < d[1]) d[1] = y; if (x > d[2]) d[2] = x; if (y > d[3]) d[3] = y; }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y); w = Math.trunc(w); h = Math.trunc(h);\r\n    if (w < 0) { x += w; w = -w; }\r\n    if (h < 0) { y += h; h = -h; }\r\n    const x0 = Math.max(0, x), y0 = Math.max(0, y), x1 = Math.min(this._width, x + w), y1 = Math.min(this._height, y + h);\r\n    if (x1 <= x0 || y1 <= y0) return;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j < y1; j++) this.fb.fill(c & 0xffff, j * this.fbw + x0, j * this.fbw + x1);\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x0, y0, x1 - 1, y1 - 1];\r\n    else { d[0] = Math.min(d[0], x0); d[1] = Math.min(d[1], y0); d[2] = Math.max(d[2], x1 - 1); d[3] = Math.max(d[3], y1 - 1); }\r\n  }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, w, 1, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, 1, h, c); }\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  /** a 16-bit colour from red, green, blue (0-255) */\r\n  color565(r, g, b) { return ((r & 0xf8) << 8) | ((g & 0xfc) << 3) | (b >> 3); }\r\n  drawRGBBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h) { for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bmp[j * w + i]); }\r\n  invertDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x21 : 0x20); }\r\n  enableDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x29 : 0x28); }\r\n  enableSleep(on) { this._send(on ? 0x10 : 0x11); }\r\n  setAddrWindow(x, y, w, h) {\r\n    this._send(0x2a, [x >> 8, x & 255, (x + w - 1) >> 8, (x + w - 1) & 255]);\r\n    this._send(0x2b, [y >> 8, y & 255, (y + h - 1) >> 8, (y + h - 1) & 255]);\r\n  }\r\n  startWrite() {}\r\n  endWrite() {}\r\n  /** the changed area, sent: a window, then its pixels (two bytes each, high byte first) */\r\n  _flush() {\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) return;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    const [x0, y0, x1, y1] = d;\r\n    const w = x1 - x0 + 1, h = y1 - y0 + 1;\r\n    this.setAddrWindow(x0, y0, w, h);\r\n    const px = new Array(w * h * 2);\r\n    let k = 0;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j <= y1; j++)\r\n      for (let i = x0; i <= x1; i++) { const c = this.fb[j * this.fbw + i]; px[k++] = c >> 8; px[k++] = c & 255; }\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([0x2c]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes(px);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7735 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(128, 160, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  initR(tab = INITR_BLACKTAB) { if (tab === INITR_MINI160x80) { this.WIDTH = 80; this.HEIGHT = 160; } this._start(); }\r\n  initB() { this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7789 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  init(w = 240, h = 320) { this.WIDTH = w; this.HEIGHT = h; this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ILI9341 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  begin() { this._start(); }\r\n  readcommand8() { return 0; }\r\n}\r\n"},"Adafruit_ILI9341.h":{"classes":["Adafruit_ILI9341"],"exports":["ILI9341_BLACK","ILI9341_NAVY","ILI9341_DARKGREEN","ILI9341_DARKCYAN","ILI9341_MAROON","ILI9341_PURPLE","ILI9341_OLIVE","ILI9341_LIGHTGREY","ILI9341_DARKGREY","ILI9341_BLUE","ILI9341_GREEN","ILI9341_CYAN","ILI9341_RED","ILI9341_MAGENTA","ILI9341_YELLOW","ILI9341_WHITE","ILI9341_ORANGE","ILI9341_GREENYELLOW","ILI9341_PINK"],"code":"// Colour TFT screens (Adafruit_ST7735.h, Adafruit_ILI9341.h, Adafruit_ST7789.h) and the Adafruit_GFX\r\n// drawing they share: fillScreen(), drawPixel(), drawLine(), drawRect(), fillRect(), drawCircle(),\r\n// fillCircle(), drawRoundRect(), drawTriangle(), setCursor(), setTextColor(c, bg), setTextSize(),\r\n// print(), setRotation(), color565(r, g, b).\r\n//   Adafruit_ST7735 tft = Adafruit_ST7735(TFT_CS, TFT_DC, TFT_RST);  tft.initR(INITR_BLACKTAB);\r\n//   Adafruit_ILI9341 tft = Adafruit_ILI9341(TFT_CS, TFT_DC);  tft.begin();\r\n// the classic 5x7 font, ASCII 32-126: five columns per character, bit 0 = the top row\r\nconst FONT5X7 = [\r\n  0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x5f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x07, 0x00, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x7f, 0x14, 0x24, 0x2a, 0x7f, 0x2a, 0x12, 0x23, 0x13, 0x08, 0x64, 0x62, 0x36, 0x49, 0x55, 0x22, 0x50, 0x00, 0x05, 0x03, 0x00, 0x00,\r\n  0x00, 0x1c, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x00, 0x08, 0x2a, 0x1c, 0x2a, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x3e, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x50, 0x30, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x00, 0x60, 0x60, 0x00, 0x00, 0x20, 0x10, 0x08, 0x04, 0x02,\r\n  0x3e, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x3e, 0x00, 0x42, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x42, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x46, 0x21, 0x41, 0x45, 0x4b, 0x31, 0x18, 0x14, 0x12, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x27, 0x45, 0x45, 0x45, 0x39, 0x3c, 0x4a, 0x49, 0x49, 0x30, 0x01, 0x71, 0x09, 0x05, 0x03,\r\n  0x36, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x06, 0x49, 0x49, 0x29, 0x1e, 0x00, 0x36, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x56, 0x36, 0x00, 0x00, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x00, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x00, 0x41, 0x22, 0x14, 0x08, 0x02, 0x01, 0x51, 0x09, 0x06,\r\n  0x32, 0x49, 0x79, 0x41, 0x3e, 0x7e, 0x11, 0x11, 0x11, 0x7e, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x36, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x22, 0x1c, 0x7f, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x01, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x49, 0x49, 0x7a,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x08, 0x08, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x41, 0x3f, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x08, 0x14, 0x22, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x7f, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x02, 0x7f, 0x7f, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x7f, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x09, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06, 0x3e, 0x41, 0x51, 0x21, 0x5e, 0x7f, 0x09, 0x19, 0x29, 0x46, 0x46, 0x49, 0x49, 0x49, 0x31, 0x01, 0x01, 0x7f, 0x01, 0x01, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x3f, 0x1f, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1f, 0x3f, 0x40, 0x38, 0x40, 0x3f,\r\n  0x63, 0x14, 0x08, 0x14, 0x63, 0x07, 0x08, 0x70, 0x08, 0x07, 0x61, 0x51, 0x49, 0x45, 0x43, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x00, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x20, 0x00, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x04, 0x02, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40, 0x40,\r\n  0x00, 0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x00, 0x20, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x78, 0x7f, 0x48, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x20, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x48, 0x7f, 0x38, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x18, 0x08, 0x7e, 0x09, 0x01, 0x02, 0x0c, 0x52, 0x52, 0x52, 0x3e,\r\n  0x7f, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x00, 0x44, 0x7d, 0x40, 0x00, 0x20, 0x40, 0x44, 0x3d, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x7f, 0x40, 0x00, 0x7c, 0x04, 0x18, 0x04, 0x78, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x78, 0x38, 0x44, 0x44, 0x44, 0x38,\r\n  0x7c, 0x14, 0x14, 0x14, 0x08, 0x08, 0x14, 0x14, 0x18, 0x7c, 0x7c, 0x08, 0x04, 0x04, 0x08, 0x48, 0x54, 0x54, 0x54, 0x20, 0x04, 0x3f, 0x44, 0x40, 0x20, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x40, 0x20, 0x7c, 0x1c, 0x20, 0x40, 0x20, 0x1c, 0x3c, 0x40, 0x30, 0x40, 0x3c,\r\n  0x44, 0x28, 0x10, 0x28, 0x44, 0x0c, 0x50, 0x50, 0x50, 0x3c, 0x44, 0x64, 0x54, 0x4c, 0x44, 0x00, 0x08, 0x36, 0x41, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x7f, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x41, 0x36, 0x08, 0x00, 0x08, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x08,\r\n];\r\nconst DEGREE = [0x00, 0x06, 0x09, 0x09, 0x06]; // (char)247 / (char)176: a degree sign\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h) {\r\n    this.WIDTH = w;\r\n    this.HEIGHT = h;\r\n    this._width = w;\r\n    this._height = h;\r\n    this.rotation = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_x = 0;\r\n    this.cursor_y = 0;\r\n    this.textsize_x = 1;\r\n    this.textsize_y = 1;\r\n    this.textcolor = 1;\r\n    this.textbgcolor = 1;\r\n    this.wrap = true;\r\n  }\r\n  width() { return this._width; }\r\n  height() { return this._height; }\r\n  getRotation() { return this.rotation; }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    this.rotation = r & 3;\r\n    const swap = this.rotation & 1;\r\n    this._width = swap ? this.HEIGHT : this.WIDTH;\r\n    this._height = swap ? this.WIDTH : this.HEIGHT;\r\n  }\r\n  setCursor(x, y) { this.cursor_x = Math.trunc(x); this.cursor_y = Math.trunc(y); }\r\n  getCursorX() { return this.cursor_x; }\r\n  getCursorY() { return this.cursor_y; }\r\n  setTextSize(sx, sy) { this.textsize_x = Math.max(1, sx | 0); this.textsize_y = Math.max(1, (sy ?? sx) | 0); }\r\n  setTextColor(c, bg) { this.textcolor = c; this.textbgcolor = bg === undefined ? c : bg; }\r\n  setTextWrap(w) { this.wrap = !!w; }\r\n  cp437() {}\r\n  setFont() {}\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  writePixel(x, y, c) { this.drawPixel(x, y, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < h; i++) this.drawPixel(x, y + i, c); }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y, c); }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) { for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawFastVLine(x + i, y, h, c); }\r\n  drawRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x, y + h - 1, w, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y, h, c);\r\n  }\r\n  drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c) {\r\n    x0 = Math.round(x0); y0 = Math.round(y0); x1 = Math.round(x1); y1 = Math.round(y1);\r\n    const dx = Math.abs(x1 - x0), dy = -Math.abs(y1 - y0), sx = x0 < x1 ? 1 : -1, sy = y0 < y1 ? 1 : -1;\r\n    let err = dx + dy;\r\n    for (;;) {\r\n      this.drawPixel(x0, y0, c);\r\n      if (x0 === x1 && y0 === y1) break;\r\n      const e2 = 2 * err;\r\n      if (e2 >= dy) { err += dy; x0 += sx; }\r\n      if (e2 <= dx) { err += dx; y0 += sy; }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    let f = 1 - r, ddx = 1, ddy = -2 * r, x = 0, y = r;\r\n    this.drawPixel(x0, y0 + r, c); this.drawPixel(x0, y0 - r, c); this.drawPixel(x0 + r, y0, c); this.drawPixel(x0 - r, y0, c);\r\n    while (x < y) {\r\n      if (f >= 0) { y--; ddy += 2; f += ddy; }\r\n      x++; ddx += 2; f += ddx;\r\n      for (const [a, b] of [[x, y], [y, x], [-x, y], [-y, x], [x, -y], [y, -x], [-x, -y], [-y, -x]]) this.drawPixel(x0 + a, y0 + b, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillCircle(x0, y0, r, c) {\r\n    for (let y = -r; y <= r; y++) {\r\n      const w = Math.floor(Math.sqrt(r * r - y * y));\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x0 - w, y0 + y, 2 * w + 1, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastHLine(x + r, y + h - 1, w - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    this.drawFastVLine(x + w - 1, y + r, h - 2 * r, c);\r\n    for (let a = 0; a <= 90; a += 3) {\r\n      const dx = Math.round(r - r * Math.cos((a * Math.PI) / 180)), dy = Math.round(r - r * Math.sin((a * Math.PI) / 180));\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + dy, c);\r\n      this.drawPixel(x + dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c); this.drawPixel(x + w - 1 - dx, y + h - 1 - dy, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRoundRect(x, y, w, h, r, c) {\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) {\r\n      const d = j < r ? r - j : j >= h - r ? j - (h - 1 - r) : 0;\r\n      const inset = d ? Math.round(r - Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, r * r - d * d))) : 0;\r\n      this.drawFastHLine(x + inset, y + j, w - 2 * inset, c);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  drawTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    this.drawLine(x0, y0, x1, y1, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x1, y1, x2, y2, c);\r\n    this.drawLine(x2, y2, x0, y0, c);\r\n  }\r\n  fillTriangle(x0, y0, x1, y1, x2, y2, c) {\r\n    const minY = Math.min(y0, y1, y2), maxY = Math.max(y0, y1, y2);\r\n    const edges = [[x0, y0, x1, y1], [x1, y1, x2, y2], [x2, y2, x0, y0]];\r\n    for (let y = minY; y <= maxY; y++) {\r\n      const xs = [];\r\n      for (const [ax, ay, bx, by] of edges) if ((y >= Math.min(ay, by)) && (y <= Math.max(ay, by)) && ay !== by) xs.push(ax + ((y - ay) * (bx - ax)) / (by - ay));\r\n      if (xs.length >= 2) { const a = Math.round(Math.min(...xs)), b = Math.round(Math.max(...xs)); this.drawFastHLine(a, y, b - a + 1, c); }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  /** a bitmap: rows of bytes, the leftmost pixel in the top bit (as the Adafruit examples' arrays) */\r\n  drawBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h, c, bg) {\r\n    const bw = Math.floor((w + 7) / 8);\r\n    for (let j = 0; j < h; j++)\r\n      for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) {\r\n        const on = (bmp[j * bw + (i >> 3)] << (i & 7)) & 0x80;\r\n        if (on) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== undefined) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bg);\r\n      }\r\n  }\r\n  drawChar(x, y, ch, c, bg, sx, sy = sx) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    const g = code === 247 || code === 176 ? DEGREE : code >= 32 && code <= 126 ? FONT5X7.slice((code - 32) * 5, (code - 32) * 5 + 5) : [0x7f, 0x41, 0x41, 0x41, 0x7f];\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {\r\n      const col = i < 5 ? g[i] : 0;\r\n      for (let j = 0; j < 8; j++) {\r\n        const on = (col >> j) & 1;\r\n        if (on) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, c);\r\n        else if (bg !== c) this.fillRect(x + i * sx, y + j * sy, sx, sy, bg);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  write(ch) {\r\n    const code = typeof ch === 'string' ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : ch;\r\n    if (code === 10) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; return 1; }\r\n    if (code === 13) return 1;\r\n    if (this.wrap && this.cursor_x + this.textsize_x * 6 > this._width) { this.cursor_x = 0; this.cursor_y += this.textsize_y * 8; }\r\n    this.drawChar(this.cursor_x, this.cursor_y, code, this.textcolor, this.textbgcolor, this.textsize_x, this.textsize_y);\r\n    this.cursor_x += this.textsize_x * 6;\r\n    return 1;\r\n  }\r\n  print(x = '', f) {\r\n    let s;\r\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && f !== undefined) s = f === 16 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(16).toUpperCase() : f === 2 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(2) : f === 8 ? Math.trunc(x).toString(8) : f === 10 ? String(Math.trunc(x)) : x.toFixed(f);\r\n    else if (typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x)) s = x.toFixed(2);\r\n    else s = String(x);\r\n    for (const ch of s) this.write(ch.charCodeAt(0) > 255 ? 63 : ch.charCodeAt(0));\r\n    return s.length;\r\n  }\r\n  println(x = '', f) { const n = this.print(x, f); this.write(10); return n + 1; }\r\n  printf(fmt, ...a) {\r\n    this.print(String(fmt).replace(/%(-?\\d*)(?:\\.(\\d+))?([dfsxXcu%])/g, (_m, w, p, t) => {\r\n      if (t === '%') return '%';\r\n      const v = a.shift();\r\n      let s = t === 'f' ? Number(v).toFixed(p ? Number(p) : 6) : t === 'x' ? Number(v).toString(16) : t === 'X' ? Number(v).toString(16).toUpperCase() : t === 'c' ? String.fromCharCode(v) : t === 'd' || t === 'u' ? String(Math.trunc(v)) : String(v);\r\n      const width = Math.abs(Number(w || 0));\r\n      if (s.length < width) s = w.startsWith('-') ? s.padEnd(width) : s.padStart(width, w.startsWith('0') ? '0' : ' ');\r\n      return s;\r\n    }));\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// The TFT drivers. Like the real libraries they talk to the controller chip over SPI: commands with\r\n// DC LOW, their data with DC HIGH (CASET / RASET set a window, RAMWR fills it with RGB565 pixels).\r\n// To be quick they draw each call (a rectangle, a line, a line of text) on the board first and send\r\n// the changed area at once, instead of pixel by pixel.\r\nconst ST77XX_BLACK = 0x0000, ST77XX_WHITE = 0xffff, ST77XX_RED = 0xf800, ST77XX_GREEN = 0x07e0, ST77XX_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ST77XX_CYAN = 0x07ff, ST77XX_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ST77XX_YELLOW = 0xffe0, ST77XX_ORANGE = 0xfc00;\r\nconst ST7735_BLACK = ST77XX_BLACK, ST7735_WHITE = ST77XX_WHITE, ST7735_RED = ST77XX_RED, ST7735_GREEN = ST77XX_GREEN, ST7735_BLUE = ST77XX_BLUE;\r\nconst ST7735_CYAN = ST77XX_CYAN, ST7735_MAGENTA = ST77XX_MAGENTA, ST7735_YELLOW = ST77XX_YELLOW, ST7735_ORANGE = ST77XX_ORANGE;\r\nconst ILI9341_BLACK = 0x0000, ILI9341_NAVY = 0x000f, ILI9341_DARKGREEN = 0x03e0, ILI9341_DARKCYAN = 0x03ef, ILI9341_MAROON = 0x7800;\r\nconst ILI9341_PURPLE = 0x780f, ILI9341_OLIVE = 0x7be0, ILI9341_LIGHTGREY = 0xc618, ILI9341_DARKGREY = 0x7bef, ILI9341_BLUE = 0x001f;\r\nconst ILI9341_GREEN = 0x07e0, ILI9341_CYAN = 0x07ff, ILI9341_RED = 0xf800, ILI9341_MAGENTA = 0xf81f, ILI9341_YELLOW = 0xffe0;\r\nconst ILI9341_WHITE = 0xffff, ILI9341_ORANGE = 0xfd20, ILI9341_GREENYELLOW = 0xafe5, ILI9341_PINK = 0xfc18;\r\nconst INITR_GREENTAB = 0x00, INITR_REDTAB = 0x01, INITR_BLACKTAB = 0x02, INITR_144GREENTAB = 0x01, INITR_MINI160x80 = 0x04;\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_SPITFT extends Adafruit_GFX {\r\n  constructor(w, h, cs, dc, a, b, c) {\r\n    super(w, h);\r\n    this.cs = cs; this.dc = dc;\r\n    // (cs, dc, rst) for hardware SPI; (cs, dc, mosi, sclk, rst) for software SPI: the same here\r\n    this.rst = c !== undefined ? c : a !== undefined && b === undefined ? a : -1;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(w * h);\r\n    this.fbw = w;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    this.depth = 0;\r\n    this.textcolor = 0xffff; this.textbgcolor = 0xffff;\r\n    // each drawing call sends what it changed when it's done (calls inside calls wait for the outer one)\r\n    for (const m of ['fillScreen', 'fillRect', 'drawRect', 'drawLine', 'drawFastHLine', 'drawFastVLine', 'drawPixel', 'drawCircle', 'fillCircle', 'drawRoundRect', 'fillRoundRect', 'drawTriangle', 'fillTriangle', 'drawBitmap', 'drawRGBBitmap', 'drawChar', 'write', 'print', 'println', 'printf']) {\r\n      const f = this[m];\r\n      this[m] = (...args) => {\r\n        this.depth++;\r\n        try { return f.apply(this, args); } finally { if (--this.depth === 0) this._flush(); }\r\n      };\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  _send(cmd, data) {\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([cmd]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    if (data && data.length) SPI.writeBytes(data);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n  _start() {\r\n    pinMode(this.cs, OUTPUT); pinMode(this.dc, OUTPUT);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n    if (this.rst >= 0) { pinMode(this.rst, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, LOW); delay(5); digitalWrite(this.rst, HIGH); delay(20); }\r\n    SPI.begin();\r\n    this._send(0x01); delay(50);      // SWRESET\r\n    this._send(0x11); delay(50);      // SLPOUT\r\n    this._send(0x3a, [0x55]);         // COLMOD: 16 bits a pixel\r\n    this.setRotation(0);\r\n    this._send(0x29);                 // DISPON\r\n  }\r\n  setRotation(r) {\r\n    super.setRotation(r);\r\n    const MAD = [0x00, 0x60, 0xc0, 0xa0][this.rotation]; // (MY MX MV: how the window maps onto the glass)\r\n    this._send(0x36, [MAD | 0x08]);   // (+ BGR order, as these panels are)\r\n    this.fbw = this._width;\r\n    this.fb = new Uint16Array(this._width * this._height);\r\n  }\r\n  drawPixel(x, y, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y);\r\n    if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= this._width || y >= this._height) return;\r\n    this.fb[y * this.fbw + x] = c & 0xffff;\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x, y, x, y];\r\n    else { if (x < d[0]) d[0] = x; if (y < d[1]) d[1] = y; if (x > d[2]) d[2] = x; if (y > d[3]) d[3] = y; }\r\n  }\r\n  fillRect(x, y, w, h, c) {\r\n    x = Math.trunc(x); y = Math.trunc(y); w = Math.trunc(w); h = Math.trunc(h);\r\n    if (w < 0) { x += w; w = -w; }\r\n    if (h < 0) { y += h; h = -h; }\r\n    const x0 = Math.max(0, x), y0 = Math.max(0, y), x1 = Math.min(this._width, x + w), y1 = Math.min(this._height, y + h);\r\n    if (x1 <= x0 || y1 <= y0) return;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j < y1; j++) this.fb.fill(c & 0xffff, j * this.fbw + x0, j * this.fbw + x1);\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) this.dirty = [x0, y0, x1 - 1, y1 - 1];\r\n    else { d[0] = Math.min(d[0], x0); d[1] = Math.min(d[1], y0); d[2] = Math.max(d[2], x1 - 1); d[3] = Math.max(d[3], y1 - 1); }\r\n  }\r\n  drawFastHLine(x, y, w, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, w, 1, c); }\r\n  drawFastVLine(x, y, h, c) { this.fillRect(x, y, 1, h, c); }\r\n  fillScreen(c) { this.fillRect(0, 0, this._width, this._height, c); }\r\n  /** a 16-bit colour from red, green, blue (0-255) */\r\n  color565(r, g, b) { return ((r & 0xf8) << 8) | ((g & 0xfc) << 3) | (b >> 3); }\r\n  drawRGBBitmap(x, y, bmp, w, h) { for (let j = 0; j < h; j++) for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) this.drawPixel(x + i, y + j, bmp[j * w + i]); }\r\n  invertDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x21 : 0x20); }\r\n  enableDisplay(on) { this._send(on ? 0x29 : 0x28); }\r\n  enableSleep(on) { this._send(on ? 0x10 : 0x11); }\r\n  setAddrWindow(x, y, w, h) {\r\n    this._send(0x2a, [x >> 8, x & 255, (x + w - 1) >> 8, (x + w - 1) & 255]);\r\n    this._send(0x2b, [y >> 8, y & 255, (y + h - 1) >> 8, (y + h - 1) & 255]);\r\n  }\r\n  startWrite() {}\r\n  endWrite() {}\r\n  /** the changed area, sent: a window, then its pixels (two bytes each, high byte first) */\r\n  _flush() {\r\n    const d = this.dirty;\r\n    if (!d) return;\r\n    this.dirty = null;\r\n    const [x0, y0, x1, y1] = d;\r\n    const w = x1 - x0 + 1, h = y1 - y0 + 1;\r\n    this.setAddrWindow(x0, y0, w, h);\r\n    const px = new Array(w * h * 2);\r\n    let k = 0;\r\n    for (let j = y0; j <= y1; j++)\r\n      for (let i = x0; i <= x1; i++) { const c = this.fb[j * this.fbw + i]; px[k++] = c >> 8; px[k++] = c & 255; }\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, LOW);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, LOW);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes([0x2c]);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.dc, HIGH);\r\n    SPI.writeBytes(px);\r\n    digitalWrite(this.cs, HIGH);\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7735 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(128, 160, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  initR(tab = INITR_BLACKTAB) { if (tab === INITR_MINI160x80) { this.WIDTH = 80; this.HEIGHT = 160; } this._start(); }\r\n  initB() { this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ST7789 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  init(w = 240, h = 320) { this.WIDTH = w; this.HEIGHT = h; this._start(); }\r\n}\r\nclass Adafruit_ILI9341 extends Adafruit_SPITFT {\r\n  constructor(cs, dc, a, b, c) { super(240, 320, cs, dc, a, b, c); }\r\n  begin() { this._start(); }\r\n  readcommand8() { return 0; }\r\n}\r\n"},"Adafruit_GFX.h":{"exports":[],"code":"// Adafruit_GFX.h: the drawing comes with each screen's own header (Adafruit_ST7735.h, Adafruit_ILI9341.h).\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"st7735","name":"Colour TFT 1.8\" (ST7735, 128x160)","description":"SPI: SCK and SDA (its MOSI) to the board's SPI pins, CS, A0 (DC: command or data) and RESET to any pins, VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, LED (backlight: to 3.3 V). #include <Adafruit_ST7735.h>; Adafruit_ST7735 tft = Adafruit_ST7735(CS, DC, RST); tft.initR(INITR_BLACKTAB); tft.fillScreen(ST77XX_BLACK);","swatch":"#141416","mass":15,"shape":[{"box":[4.4,0.16,5.8],"at":[0,0.08,-0.25],"color":"#c83030"},{"box":[3.6,0.3,4.6],"at":[0,0.31,0],"color":"#141416"},{"screen":{"id":"tft","size":[2.85,3.55],"px":[128,160],"mode":"rgb","bg":"#000000"},"at":[0,0.462,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["LED","SCK","SDA","A0","RESET","CS","GND","VCC"],"at":[-0.889,0,-2.8],"kinds":{"LED":"in","SCK":"in","SDA":"in","A0":"in","RESET":"in","CS":"in","GND":"gnd","VCC":"vin"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.8,"vmax":5.5},"SDA":{"label":"SDA (its MOSI)"},"A0":{"label":"A0 (DC: data / command)"},"RESET":{"pulled":"up"},"LED":{"label":"LED (backlight)","pulled":"up"}}}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"SDA","cs":"CS"},"device":"st7735"},{"id":"ili9341","name":"Colour TFT 2.8\" (ILI9341, 240x320)","description":"SPI: SCK, MOSI (and MISO) to the board's SPI pins, CS, DC and RESET to any pins, VCC (3.3-5 V), GND, LED (backlight: to 3.3 V). #include <Adafruit_ILI9341.h>; Adafruit_ILI9341 tft = Adafruit_ILI9341(CS, DC, RST); tft.begin(); tft.fillScreen(ILI9341_BLACK);","swatch":"#141416","mass":40,"shape":[{"box":[5,0.16,8.6],"at":[0,0.08,-0.4],"color":"#c83030"},{"box":[4.6,0.35,6.6],"at":[0,0.335,0],"color":"#141416"},{"screen":{"id":"tft","size":[4.32,5.76],"px":[240,320],"mode":"rgb","bg":"#000000"},"at":[0,0.512,0]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","CS","RESET","DC","MOSI","SCK","LED","MISO"],"at":[-1.016,0,-4.4],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","CS":"in","RESET":"in","DC":"in","MOSI":"in","SCK":"in","LED":"in","MISO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2.8,"vmax":5.5},"DC":{"label":"DC (data / command)"},"RESET":{"pulled":"up"},"LED":{"label":"LED (backlight)","pulled":"up"}}}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"MOSI","miso":"MISO","cs":"CS"},"device":"ili9341"}],"examples":[{"name":"Colour dashboard","description":"A 2.8\" ILI9341 shows a dashboard: a title bar, the knob's value as a gauge and a moving graph. Press Run and turn the knob (its slider in the run panel).","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Colour dashboard","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-12,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"tft","type":"tft-displays/ili9341","name":"Screen","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[5,0,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071],"pinned":true},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Knob","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-12,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"LED"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP17"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"CS"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"DC"},"color":"#9b59b6"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"RESET"},"color":"#f2f2f2"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP18"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"SCK"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP19"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"MOSI"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP16"},"b":{"uid":"tft","pin":"MISO"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Colour dashboard on a 2.8\" ILI9341: a title bar, the knob as a gauge and a scrolling graph.\n#include <SPI.h>\n#include <Adafruit_GFX.h>\n#include <Adafruit_ILI9341.h>\n\n#define TFT_CS 17\n#define TFT_DC 14\n#define TFT_RST 15\n#define KNOB A0\n\nAdafruit_ILI9341 tft = Adafruit_ILI9341(TFT_CS, TFT_DC, TFT_RST);\nint x = 0;\nint lastY = -1;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  tft.begin();\n  tft.setRotation(1);                  // landscape: 320 x 240\n  tft.fillScreen(ILI9341_BLACK);\n  tft.fillRect(0, 0, 320, 30, ILI9341_NAVY);\n  tft.setTextColor(ILI9341_WHITE);\n  tft.setTextSize(2);\n  tft.setCursor(10, 8);\n  tft.print(\"Bench dashboard\");\n  tft.drawRect(10, 40, 300, 40, ILI9341_LIGHTGREY);\n  tft.drawRect(10, 100, 300, 130, ILI9341_DARKGREY);\n  Serial.println(\"drawn\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int raw = analogRead(KNOB);                  // 0 .. 4095\n  int pct = map(raw, 0, 4095, 0, 100);\n  // the gauge: a bar and the number\n  int w = map(pct, 0, 100, 0, 296);\n  uint16_t colour = pct < 50 ? ILI9341_GREEN : pct < 80 ? ILI9341_YELLOW : ILI9341_RED;\n  tft.fillRect(12, 42, w, 36, colour);\n  tft.fillRect(12 + w, 42, 296 - w, 36, ILI9341_BLACK);\n  tft.setTextColor(ILI9341_WHITE, ILI9341_BLACK);\n  tft.setCursor(250, 52);\n  tft.setTextSize(2);\n  tft.print(pct);\n  tft.print(\"% \");\n  // the graph: a column at a time, wrapping round\n  int y = map(pct, 0, 100, 227, 103);\n  tft.drawFastVLine(12 + x, 102, 126, ILI9341_BLACK);\n  if (lastY >= 0) tft.drawLine(11 + x, lastY, 12 + x, y, ILI9341_CYAN);\n  lastY = y;\n  x = (x + 2) % 296;\n  if (x == 0) lastY = -1;\n  delay(50);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}